                <pb facs="0870" n="758" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg758"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Consul Moffat to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.:]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bluefields</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-08-20"><hi rendition="#italic">August 20,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Moffat reports that the Madriz forces under Gen. Rivas, numbering 700,
                    attacked and were defeated by Mena at Granada; that the attack resulted in
                    complete rout; and that Rivas was killed. Adds that the revolutionaries intend
                    immediate advance upon Masaya.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
